03chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nHow can you reproduce this bug? We have a much better chance at fixing issues if we can reproduce them!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e…\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e…\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e…\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nWhat is meant to happen here that isn’t working correctly?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nIf applicable, attach images or videos (.jpg, .png, .gif, .mp4, .mov)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOperating System\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"48:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Windows 10/11\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"49:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e MacOS\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"50:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Linux\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVersion Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor Cursor IDE: Menu → About Cursor → Copy\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor Cursor CLI: Run \u003ccode\u003eagent about\u003c/code\u003e in your terminal\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eIDE:\nVersion: 2.xx.x\nVSCode Version: 1.105.1\nCommit: ......\n\nCLI:\nCLI Version 2026.01.17-d239e66\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nModel name (e.g., Sonnet 4, Tab…)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nRequest ID: f9a7046a-279b-47e5-ab48-6e8dc12daba1\u003cbr\u003e\nFor Background Agent issues, also post the ID: bc-…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nAdd any other context about the problem here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"87:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Yes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"88:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Sometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"89:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e No - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe more details you provide, the easier it is for us to reproduce and fix the issue. Thanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-13T07:45:01.525Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171479,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-repeatedly-disconnects-and-gets-stuck-on-reconnecting-during-active-sessions","display_username":"system","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/agents","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":-1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-repeatedly-disconnects-and-gets-stuck-on-reconnecting-during-active-sessions/171479/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":489928,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-13T10:03:15.173Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/turtle1\"\u003e@TURTLE1\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report, and sorry for the trouble.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYyour Agent Computer itself is healthy on our side and your bots are safe. What is failing is the lookup your PC does to find the computer’s address. From what we can see, the DNS on your network (Reliance Jio) is timing out or returning “not found” for that address most of the time, which is exactly when the app shows “Reconnecting” and “Showing saved messages”. The lookup happens on your network, so Retry, Recover and Reset do not fix it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease try these steps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot (right-click the tray icon and choose Quit).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Windows Settings, then Network and internet.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick your active connection (Wi-Fi or Ethernet), then click Edit next to “DNS server assignment”.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChoose Manual, turn on IPv4, enter 1.1.1.1 as Preferred DNS and 8.8.8.8 as Alternate DNS, and click Save.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot again and use it for 15 to 20 minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-13T10:03:20.388Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":10.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171479,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-repeatedly-disconnects-and-gets-stuck-on-reconnecting-during-active-sessions","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-repeatedly-disconnects-and-gets-stuck-on-reconnecting-during-active-sessions/171479/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[489795,489796,489928]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot repeatedly disconnects and gets stuck on “Reconnecting” during active sessions","id":171479,"title":"Grok Bot repeatedly disconnects and gets stuck on “Reconnecting” during active sessions","posts_count":3,"created_at":"2026-09-13T07:44:53.806Z","views":34,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-13T10:03:15.173Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"grok-bot-repeatedly-disconnects-and-gets-stuck-on-reconnecting-during-active-sessions","category_id":6,"word_count":690,"de